  "body": "Closes #919\nClaim: cloud/i919-sonnet\n\n## Problem\n\nThe survey did not ask which experimental options (#903) members want by default, and D1 listed the sidebar sections as text only, although the cards exist since #914.\n\n## Change\n\n- **X1**: new multiple-choice question, wording and ids as proposed in #919, on its own screen after D2 and before the cards, no condition (iPhone profiles see it too). `aucune` is exclusive (checking it unchecks the others and the reverse).\n- New question type `choix-multiple` (the only architecture addition, needed because every existing choice is single): stored as a list of codes in `questions.md` order; the question's `exclusive` field names the exclusive code. Validation (also used by `--corriger`), stats (each code counted over the respondents of the question, so shares do not sum to 100), analysis export (one column, codes joined by a space) and the end-screen comparison handle it.\n- `questions.md` (new « Choix multiple » line and reading rule), `cadrage-construction.md` §2 (row, budgets 6 min 55 s / 4 min 55 s) and `formulaire-spec.md` (type list) updated. `donnees.md` unchanged: only answer ids are stored, no new kind of data.\n- **D1 cards**: the 9 cards are copied to `web/visuels/D1-cartes/` (embedded in the binary), referenced by each D1 section in `questionnaire.json` with the alt text of `inventaire.md`, and shown next to each section's state. Sort and order behaviour unchanged; one image per section is moved, not recreated, on re-sort. CSP unchanged (`img-src 'self'`).\n\n## Tests\n\n- Go: concordance (`TestConcordanceX1`, « Choix multiple » line vs type and exclusive code, D1 cards byte-identical to `docs/`), loader refusals, validation (exclusivity, unknown/duplicate code, order, empty list, `ValiderUne`), stats, export.\n- JS (`node --test`, 16 pass): X1 screen position, check/uncheck/exclusive, sending and clearing, comparison; D1 cards: nine, files present, order follows the sort.\n- `go vet ./...`, `go test -race ./...`, `node --test`, markdownlint-cli2 0.18.1: green. Also checked in headless Chromium against the built binary: 9 cards loaded, X1 exclusivity, full submission, no console error.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CFXdrTPRGCMAjRetfa)_",
