   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, read-only sub-agent of cloud/orch; the author is Sonnet), verbatim:**\n\n> APPROVE\n>\n> **Adversarial review (Opus 5.5): APPROVE**, head 13234f3f\n>\n> Findings (none blocking):\n>\n> 1. Low, `tooling/ux-survey/web/logique.js:148`: `d1Cartes` is used only by the tests. The two D1 tests (\"neuf cartes…\" and \"les cartes suivent le tri\") check this helper, not the code the respondent sees: `app.js` `dessiner()` loops over `d1Affichage` and calls `vignetteSection`. Failing scenario: someone breaks the card wiring in `app.js` (for example, the wrong section key in the `vignettes` cache), and every test stays green. Fix: have `dessiner()` loop over `L.d1Cartes(contenu, d1)`, or remove `d1Cartes` and test `d1Carte` together with `d1Affichage`.\n> 2. Low, `docs/ux/questionnaire/visuels/inventaire.md:49`: this line still says \"Le formulaire présente aujourd'hui les sections en texte : ces cartes servent au test à cinq…\". This PR makes it false (L08/L09). Update the sentence.\n> 3. Detail, `tooling/ux-survey/contenu/questionnaire.json` (D1 `sections[].visuels[].alt`): the alt texts were copied from the inventory with their Markdown backticks and SF Symbol names (`` `star.fill` ``, `` `gearshape` ``). A screen reader reads these out to respondents. Fix: write respondent-facing alt texts, e.g. \"Carte « Favoris » : étoile, aujourd'hui dans le groupe Forum\".\n>\n> Checked and correct:\n> - X1's wording, codes, help text, position (after D2, before the cards, no condition) and budget all match #919.\n> - `aucune` is exclusive on both sides: `validerMultiple` on the server (also reached through `ValiderUne`, R7) and `cocherCode` in the browser.\n> - The server rejects unknown codes, duplicates and non-arrays. The 6-code list and the request size limit (`MaxBytesReader`) bound the length. Codes are stored in the order of `questions.md`, and an empty list is not stored.\n> - `donnees.md` needs no change: X1 stores choice codes only, which \"Vos réponses aux questions\" already covers.\n> - The concordance test checks the \"Choix multiple\" line against `exclusive`, and `TestConcordanceX1` checks the codes, the screen and the order.\n> - The D1 cards are byte-identical copies, embedded and served by the binary (`WalkDir` + `//go:embed web`). The CSP is unchanged (`img-src 'self'`).\n> - No XSS: `h()` sets attributes with `setAttribute` and text with text nodes, and the content is static.\n>\n> **Verified**: ran `go vet ./...` and `go test -race ./...` (all packages ok) and `node --test web/logique.test.mjs` (16/16) on the head. The tests fail without the change: with the server-side `aucune` check removed, `TestChoixMultipleX1` fails twice; with the browser-side `choix.delete(q.exclusive)` removed, 1 JS test fails.\n\nThe three items reach respondents (screen reader) or the docs. cloud/orch asks `cloud/i919-sonnet` for one cleanup commit, followed by a short Opus delta review, before the merge.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
