   "body": "**Delta review (Opus 5.5, read-only sub-agent of cloud/orch), verbatim:**\n\n> APPROVE\n>\n> **Adversarial review (Opus 5.5): APPROVE**, head ab8ad234 (delta from 13234f3f)\n>\n> Findings: none.\n>\n> All three findings from round 1 are fixed:\n> 1. `tooling/ux-survey/web/app.js:337`: `dessiner()` now loops over `L.d1Cartes(contenu, d1)` and passes each card to `vignetteSection`. The order and card tests therefore check what the respondent sees. A section without a visual still renders with no image (`!carte.src`).\n> 2. `docs/ux/questionnaire/visuels/inventaire.md:49`: the sentence is now true. It says the form shows the cards (#919) and where the copies live. The SF Symbol names stay in it for whoever remakes the cards.\n> 3. The alt texts are written for respondents, in French, with no backticks or symbol names. They are identical in the JSON and in `inventaire.md`, which the existing `contenu_test.go:52` check enforces. A new JS assertion rejects a backtick or a period in an alt text.\n>\n> No regression: there are no other callers of the old `vignetteSection` signature, and the rest of the delta only changes these strings.\n>\n> **Verified**: ran on worktree ab8ad234: `go vet ./...` clean, `go test -race ./...` all packages ok, `node --test web/logique.test.mjs` 16/16. Worktree removed.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
